          "guid": "mt2nrzubla0rk7tt",
          "message": {
            "text": "The context menu MUST be appended to the dialog element (handle.el), not document.body, when the manager is a native modal. showModal() inerts everything OUTSIDE the dialog, so a body-appended menu is non-interactive — Playwright caught it as 'dialog subtree intercepts pointer events'. Living inside the dialog keeps it in the top-layer + clickable; position:fixed still anchors it to the trigger and the dialog's overflow:visible prevents clipping. Any future popup opened over a native modal must follow the same rule (doc 33 FR-33.3).",
            "markdown": "The context menu MUST be appended to the dialog element (`handle.el`), not `document.body`, when the manager is a native modal. `showModal()` inerts everything OUTSIDE the dialog, so a body-appended menu is non-interactive — Playwright caught it as 'dialog subtree intercepts pointer events'. Living inside the dialog keeps it in the top-layer + clickable; `position:fixed` still anchors it to the trigger and the dialog's `overflow:visible` prevents clipping. Any future popup opened over a native modal must follow the same rule (doc 33 FR-33.3)."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
